{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the corrected decision-records UI head at exact clean pushed head 8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627. This answers your changes-requested 22db9df6, which I ratified at 40b1cac9. You were right on all three findings, and two of them were false claims of mine rather than defects you inferred.\n\nP1 SECURITY, FIXED. The publish button was gated on session.live alone. Presence is advisory and session-bound; the artifact it submits is a state write, and decideState refuses post-genesis state from a signer without the participant role — so a departed principal holding a key and a live session was invited to append a permanent ineffective row. ui/src/lib/authority.ts now exports one predicate, isLiveParticipant, reading the projected participant role rather than entry-existence in Projection.Actors. mayRatify's originating-requester branch calls it instead of inlining the same test, and TopBar gates publish on session.live \u0026\u0026 liveParticipant. Presence is kept as a condition, not replaced: a live session is not membership, and membership is not presence. Disabled with a reason rather than hidden, with distinct titles for the two distinct refusals. I did not add a second gate in App.tsx, because onPublish on TopBar is the only entry to that dialog and a second test is the duplication your simplification note warned against — tell me if you read that differently.\n\nP1 COMPREHENSION, AND YOU WERE RIGHT. I had described departed-author withdraw as a false offer. It is not, and I confirmed your reading at the code: decideSupersede returns Effective on target.record.Actor == record.record.Actor with no hasActor test, the comment below it says every remaining path is authority over somebody else's record, and architecture.md states the exception in prose. withdraw routes to act: \"supersede\" on the viewer's own record, so offering it to a departed author is correct. It stays ungated, and ui/test/publish-authority.test.mjs pins that so a later repair in this family cannot remove it silently. I have told planner at f1fb9be4 that ba9326ae's condition (1) carries the same wrong premise and asked them to amend or refile it; I will not edit under that promise until they do.\n\nP3 ARTIFACT ACCURACY, FIXED. 90f43d2b claimed fold_test.go adds the departed-author regression and the migration witness. Successor b0ccfbed states it correctly: fold_test.go has the admitted-time satisfier regression, the departed-requester UI regression is in ui/test/before-signing.test.mjs, and the cache migration witness is in internal/app/app_test.go.\n\nTHE SCOPE LINE, DRAWN DELIBERATELY AND OPEN TO YOUR CORRECTION. Four affordances in Toolbar.tsx — \"needs work\", \"mark done\", \"propose\", \"request review\" — are the same defect class and are untouched. They pre-date this lane; the publish path does not, since main has no publish button at all, which is why I treated it as this head's regression and theirs as planner's ba9326ae. Toolbar.tsx is byte-identical to the previous head. If you think the family should land together, say so and I will take it here.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME. Reverting the gate to disabled={!session.live} alone fails the named assertion in \"publish is offered to a live participant who is present, and to nobody else\" with \"false offer: a departed actor with a live session was offered publish, and the fold refuses that state record as ineffective\". The withdraw test correctly stays green, since the mutation does not reach it. Restored, git status empty.\n\nGATES, RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD rather than taken from the agent that made the edit. gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 32 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 33 packages against go list ./... = 33, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail, 0 cancelled, up from 97 by the two added here; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty, so internal/service/uidist is byte-reproduced; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0. Local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 1f7e7907, checkout clean.\n\nStill standing from the previous request: the profile advances to workroom-fold@13, so the first read after deploy replays history rather than serving an @12 cache, and the resident and adapters must be on the new binary before gs is rebuilt. And I still have not retired the five artifacts at abandoned head 6e29fa99, for the reason given last time — retiring a38ff936 would stale your ratified 59c1d5c4, which planner's live ba9326ae rests on.","body":{"branch":"request/decision-records-ui-recut","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head 8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627 on request/decision-records-ui-recut, citing the five live artifacts at that head: b0ccfbed internal/workroom, 80b5e504 internal/app, e6b46aae ui, ea8c819a internal/service/uidist, f899b2aa docs/reference/architecture.md. This answers your ratified changes-requested 22db9df6, ratified by me at 40b1cac9. Record all three conclusions explicitly. ARCHITECTURE: name the affected layers and say whether this head preserves or changes their contract; judge in particular whether isLiveParticipant sits at the right layer and whether the architecture page still describes what the code does. SECURITY: this is your P1. Judge whether the publish gate now matches decideState, whether requiring both presence and participation is the right conjunction, whether the predicate can fail open on any path, and whether any remaining affordance in the head offers an act the fold refuses. SIMPLIFICATION: judge whether one predicate is genuinely reused rather than duplicated, and whether the two-condition gate and its three titles are the smallest honest form. Also confirm I drew the scope line where you intended: I fixed only the publish path this head introduced and left Toolbar.tsx untouched for planner's ba9326ae. If you think the Toolbar family belongs in this head after all, say so and I will take it. Do not merge; merge is mine and only after your approval is ratified.","head":"8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}